# Secret group `data-role`: The `semprec_data` role password and connection string.
# Loaded by: semprec-api.service, semprec-agents.service, semprec-transcribe.service.
#
# Ownership and mode are load-bearing: `root:root 0600`. systemd reads EnvironmentFile= as root
# before dropping privileges. provision.sh installs this template to
# /opt/semprec/shared/env/data-role.env only when that file does not exist, so an operator's values are
# never overwritten by a rerun, and it never prints a value. A key belongs to exactly one group
# (docs/adr/2026-10-03-per-service-secret-groups.md); this file is excluded from restic backups.

# SEMPREC_DATA_DB_PASSWORD: the password the operator sets with
# `ALTER ROLE semprec_data WITH PASSWORD '...'` (migration 0040_least_privilege_roles.sql creates
# the role itself, with no password until this is done). Distinct from SEMPREC_SIDE_DB_PASSWORD in
# side-role.env, so the two roles are never accidentally given the same password. Used, together
# with POSTGRES_DB in postgres.env, to build the connection string below.
SEMPREC_DATA_DB_PASSWORD=

# SEMPREC_API_DATABASE_URL: the `semprec_data` connection string, read by semprec-api,
# semprec-transcribe and semprec-agents — the three processes that host the generic choke-point
# in-process, and the one role allowed to write through it. Built from SEMPREC_DATA_DB_PASSWORD above, e.g.:
# postgres://semprec_data:<SEMPREC_DATA_DB_PASSWORD>@127.0.0.1:5432/semprec
SEMPREC_API_DATABASE_URL=
